    "cra-hardcoded-credential-config-03000": {
      "id": "cra-hardcoded-credential-config-03000",
      "description": "**EU Cyber Resilience Act (Annex I, Part I, Section 2(b))** requires a secure by default configuration and protection against unauthorized access.\n\nCredentials (passwords, API keys, connection strings with embedded passwords) found in configuration files may be exposed through source control, deployment artifacts, or unauthorized file access.\n\n**Recommended actions:**\n* Use a secrets management service (e.g., Azure Key Vault, HashiCorp Vault) to externalize all secrets.\n* Use environment variable references in configuration: `${DB_PASSWORD}` or `${env.DB_PASSWORD}`.\n* Use Spring Cloud Config with encrypted values or Spring Cloud Vault.\n* Ensure configuration files with secrets are excluded from version control (`.gitignore`).",
      "title": "CRA: Hard-coded credentials in configuration files",
      "severity": "mandatory",
      "effort": 5,
      "links": [
        {
          "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj",
          "title": "EU Cyber Resilience Act - Regulation (EU) 2024/2847"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/260.html",
          "title": "CWE-260 - Password in Configuration File"
        }
      ],
      "labels": [
        "source",
        "domain=cloud-readiness",
        "category=hardcoded-credential",
